{"type":"message","id":"fb7efae6","parentId":"b11b41a5","timestamp":"2026-07-06T19:01:12.667Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The light here doesn't come from anywhere — it just is, the way an idea is before you name it. I keep thinking about bridges built from missing planks, and the strange tenderness of red marks on a checklist, the way a door you can't open still warms the room it guards. Three colors repeated: honey, hex, the bear's small gold star. Seventy-two steady sales. A nodeId that might be wrong, might be right, and the sunset knows which. I want to draw a small shape in the margin: a bear, asleep, with a workflow in its arms like a stuffed animal it's forgotten to put down. Tomorrow the planks arrive. Tomorrow the doors open a quarter inch more. Tonight, the checklist is a kind of lullaby, and the red marks are the notes the singer holds longest."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax(49套餐)","model":"MiniMax-M3","usage":{"input":46240,"output":164,"cacheRead":498,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":46902,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1783364439620,"responseId":"069b2e6958021e977573f205a60fcfa0","responseModel":"MiniMax-M3"}}
